a"},{"id":"b","text":"Wrong timing of computation"},{"id":"c","text":"Changes of prices of goods within the year"},{"id":"d","text":"Double counting"}],"correctOptionId":"d","source":"TestDriller WAEC past questions","sourceUrl":"https://www.testdriller.com/past-questions/waec-objective-economics-2010-31","topic":"National Income & Accounting"},{"id":"waec-economics-2010-q032","exam":"WAEC","subject":"Economics","year":2010,"prompt":"The total stock of money available for us in an economy is","options":[{"id":"a","text":"a function of money"},{"id":"b","text":"a characteristic of money"},{"id":"c","text":"the demand for money"},{"id":"d","text":"the supply of money"}],"correctOptionId":"d","source":"TestDriller WAEC past questions","sourceUrl":"https://www.testdriller.com/past-questions/waec-objective-economics-2010-32","topic":"Money, Banking & Finance"},{"id":"waec-economics-2010-q033","exam":"WAEC","subject":"Economics","year":2010,"prompt":"Which of the following is not a reason for holding money?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Ostentation"},{"id":"b","text":"Speculation"},{"id":"c","text":"Transactions"},{"id":"d","text":"Precautionary"}],"correctOptionId":"a","source":"TestDriller WAEC past questions","sourceUrl":"https://www.testdriller.com/past-questions/waec-objective-economics-2010-33","topic":"Money, Banking & Finance"},{"id":"waec-economics-2010-q034","exam":"WAEC","subject":"Economics","year":2010,"prompt":"The best way of combating demand - pull inflation is to","options":[{"id":"a","text":"increase income taxes"},{"id":"b","text":"reduce income taxes"},{"id":"c","text":"increase import duties"},{"id":"d","text":"increase salaries and wages"}],"correctOptionId":"a","source":"TestDriller WAEC past questions","sourceUrl":"https://www.testdriller.com/past-questions/waec-objective-economics-2010-34","topic":"International Trade & Finance"},{"id":"waec-economics-2010-q035","exam":"WAEC","subject":"Economics","year":2010,"prompt":"In which of the following wa